WEBVTT

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.810
The Pokémon World Championships,
Hyper Class...

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.860
Satoshi is currently ranked 64th.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.990
For his second battle,
he faces Galar Gym Leader Saito,

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:19.370
who he previously battled twice in the Super Class;
first to a loss, then to a draw.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.750
In the middle
of their intense match,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.550
the stadium received a visit from
none other than Champion Dande,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.960
the ultimate goal
Satoshi and Saito wish to reach.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.960
The match between Satoshi and Saito rages on
without a clear winner in sight.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.310
Who will be the victor?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.420
And it lands!

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:41.940
Thinking impressively fast,

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.860
Lucario put its strength into its legs
to counter having its arms blocked!

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.110
The crowd goes wild!

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.420
Return, Lucario!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.660
Go, Negigaknight!

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.960
Contestant Satoshi’s third pick
is Negigaknight.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.250
It takes a stance that combines
both attack and defense!

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.050
That Lucario’s incredible.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:14.870
And he went with Negigaknight...
I thought he’d pick Kairyu...

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:19.260
He’s facing her head on.
He wants to beat Saitokins with his own Fighting types!

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.830
Man, what a heated battle.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.730
Kyodaimax and Mega Evolution...
When do you think they’ll use them, Mr. Dande?

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.080
Shh.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:31.290
Right now, I’m enjoying this battle
from the bottom of my heart.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.460
You should sit back
and enjoy your role.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:36.530
Consecutive Cut!

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.490
Bullet Punch!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.170
All right!

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.330
Come back to me, Kairiky.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.810
Go, Luchabull!

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.110
Flying Press!

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.160
Crossroad Kill!

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:27.210
Jump!

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.810
That Luchabull moved fast!

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.340
It dodged Negigaknight!

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.540
Brutal Swing!

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.800
And it tossed the shield!
What a new and inspired Brutal Swing!

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.890
God Bird!

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:48.770
Now, Luchabull has started
storing up energy for God Bird!

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.270
Now! Crossroad Kill!

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:09.960
Negigaknight!

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.590
Negigaknight is unable to battle.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.130
Contestant Saito
takes the first point!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.180
A knockout blow
from Luchabull’s God Bird clinched it!

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.330
Return!

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:32.480
You did your best.
Now rest up.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.480
Pikachu, you’re up!

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.870
To replace the downed Negigaknight,
he sends in Pikachu!

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.410
God Bird!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.620
100,000 Volts!

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.760
Iron Tail!

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:06.760
Dig into the ground!

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.060
What...?!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.300
Luchabull...

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.060
Take him out!

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.110
Lightning Speed!

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:31.260
The power of the Lightning Speed
is making Pikachu’s body shake violently!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.540
What could this be?!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:45.470
In a stunning turn of events, Pikachu took
the God Bird that finished Negigaknight off!

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:49.140
Still, they both took
heavy damage...

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.270
He had even more crazy tricks...

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:57.660
Back when he fended off Ms. Visquez’s attack
at Kuchiba Gym, he only used Iron Tail.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.340
Why would he use
Lightning Speed?

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:03.890
He used its speed
to create ultrasonic vibrations.

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:04.990
Ultrasonic vibrations?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.040
Yeah.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:12.200
He took less damage from God Bird,
and even dealt some damage in return.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.580
You astonish me,
trainer of Lucario.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.830
It’s Satoshi!

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.040
Are you always training
to use moves like these?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.070
I just come up with stuff
when I’m battling someone!

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:27.560
My head heats up
and goes all “boom” with ideas!

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.700
Without any planning?

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.350
You impress me
with these improvised tactics,

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.850
but your Pikachu impresses me
even more by pulling them off.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:40.760
Defeating you will certainly
grant me great insights.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.820
Luchabull! High Jump Kick!

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.780
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.730
The 100,000 Volts hit their mark!
It’s super effective!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.430
Luchabull is unable to battle!

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.680
We did it, Pikachu!

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.930
Now, they’re down to
two Pokémon each!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.940
Luchabull, come back to me.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:23.280
Otosupus...
I ask for your aid!

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.760
Pikachu, can you keep going?

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:34.850
What kind of battle
are we in for now?

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:37.410
Otosupus versus Pikachu!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.420
Lightning Speed!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:42.840
Octolock!

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:48.090
The Lightning Speed strikes!

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:51.760
What?!

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.020
Pikachu has been trapped!

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.520
You won’t get out of this again.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:08:59.980
100,000 Volts!

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:07.860
Is the Octolock making it so Pikachu
can’t find its strength?

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.610
The 100,000 Volts fizzle out!

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.720
When he’s caught,
he’s done for...

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.500
That Octolock
is an ugly move to deal with...

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.200
No good, huh?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.350
Pikachu!
Struggling won’t work!

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.270
Relax all your muscles!

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.130
Give in to Otosupus!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.640
That won’t work.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:30.590
Otosupus! Infight!

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.820
Pikachu!

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.570
Pikachu is unable to battle!

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:00.800
Now, Contestant Satoshi
only has one Pokémon left.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.520
You did great. Thanks.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.430
She really is strong...

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:15.300
But...

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:21.270
We’re gonna win this!

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:23.940
Lucario, I choose you!

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:30.770
I won’t settle for a draw again,
Otosupus.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:31.820
Be careful.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:41.400
If this drags on,
it won’t have any strength left to face Kairiky...

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.830
We’ll finish this in one blow!

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:55.630
It’s a staring match
between the two sides.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.010
Which one
will make the first move?!

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.180
Aqua Break!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:07.310
Aura Sphere!

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.260
Otosupus is unable to battle!

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.390
You did it, Lucario!

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.770
What a piercing fighting spirit!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.600
Lucario wins
the breathtaking exchange!

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:57.780
He won!
He actually beat that Otosupus, Sarunori!

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:03.040
This’ll be the last match-up,
Saitokins...

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.870
I give you my thanks,
Otosupus.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.940
It’s time to dig in our heels!
I’ll give this everything I’ve got!

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.250
I ask for your aid, Kairiky!

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.740
Now, they both have
only one Pokémon left.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.510
Kairiky versus Lucario!

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:28.270
Kairiky and Lucario have both taken
considerable damage so far.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:38.440
Kairiky.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:48.040
I can’t recall the last time
a battle made me so excited.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.460
She’s smiling?!

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.800
Fine then,
let’s just destroy everything!

00:12:56.460 --> 00:13:00.430
Your skill is worthy of respect—
and Kyodaimaxing!

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:16.900
There it is!

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.210
We’re finally getting to see
Kairiky’s Kyodaimax!

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:32.420
So outrageously huge!
Now <i>this</i> is a Galarian Battle!

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.490
That’s her true ace?!

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:37.170
It’s as overwhelming as ever.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.970
Now, it’s your turn.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.550
Let’s go, Lucario!

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.030
Let’s go, Lucario!

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.380
The bond between us...

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.450
Mega Evolve!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.400
This Hyper Class battle
has been intense!

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.570
Contestant Saito
versus Contestant Satoshi!

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:41.240
No... Kyodaimax
versus Mega Evolution!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.500
Aura Sphere!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:49.660
Dai Steel!

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:06.140
The powers of Mega Evolution
and Kyodaimax collide!

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:07.590
They’re evenly matched!

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:10.560
Force Palm!

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.810
Dai Attack!

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:28.030
The Dai Attack lands!

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:30.660
Lucario,
keep going with Force Palm!

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:39.380
It’s unbelievable! Even after taking the Dai Attack,
Lucario bravely keeps up the offensive!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.340
Both sides have endured
yet another hit!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:50.350
Kairiky!
Increase your Daimax Power!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:54.610
Power is gathering in Kairiky’s fist!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.480
Here it comes, Lucario!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.410
I’ll use karate along with
my partner’s move, acting as one!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.940
Kyodai Focus Blow!

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:17.290
That move’s the reason
Saitokins and Kairiky have been on a roll.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.250
Lucario! Hold on!

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.450
It withstood the attack...

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.270
Lucario, jump!

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:47.930
Contestant Satoshi strikes back!

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:52.030
Amazing!
It’s running up Kairiky’s massive body!

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.870
Aura Sphere!

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:10.060
Mega Lucario took down the giant!

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:13.100
A world-shaking spectacle!

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:13.970
All right!

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:18.400
Good work, Lucario!

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:20.480
This is where things get scary.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:31.540
Kairiky is back to normal size,
but its enhanced power remains!

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:34.320
Rush in, Lucario!

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:43.290
Right now, Kairiky can strike critical points
with unmatched accuracy!

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:50.880
Bullet Punch!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.020
Lucario!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:03.810
Force Palm!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:13.700
Go!

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.420
What’s this?!

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.340
Steely Resolve!

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:44.230
Lucario’s Steely Resolve erupts!

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:07.670
Kairiky is unable to battle.
Lucario wins!

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:10.670
As such,
the winner is Contestant Satoshi!

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:16.680
The fierce battle is over!
And what an awe-inspiring battle it was!

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.760
We won...

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.450
We did it.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.190
Lucario!

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.360
You okay?

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:36.360
You did great.

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.540
Based on the results of this battle,

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:45.360
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:51.960
Contestant Satoshi emerges victorious over
Contestant Saito, and rises to 36th in the Hyper Class!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.660
36th!

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:57.470
Satoshi, Lucario, Pikachu, Negigaknight...
You’re incredible!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:01.210
You actually beat Saitokins...

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:03.890
How strong are you gonna get,
Satoshi?

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:07.980
Kairiky.
That was a good battle.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:09.100
You have my gratitude.

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:21.470
In celebration of their daring fight,
the stadium is filled with claps and cheers!

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:27.410
Mr. Dande,
what did you think of today’s battle?

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.490
I wish I could’ve seen even more.

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:39.460
Congrats, Satoshi.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:42.720
You’re ranked 36th!
That’s amazing!

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:47.380
Mr. Dande was watching me.
No way I wasn’t gonna get fired up.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.870
But... he went and left
right away...

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.310
No, this is for the best.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:58.950
We should only meet him
upon the battlefield.

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:06.580
During our bout today,
I realized my heart was dancing.

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:13.260
I won’t be throwing in the towel.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.840
Someday, let us battle again...
Satoshi.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:22.540
Looking forward to it,
Ms. Saito!

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:23.970
Just Saito is fine!

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.720
Okay, Saito!

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.150
That means Ms. Saito...

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.890
...acknowledged Satoshi!

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:35.880
Satoshi and Saito’s Hyper Class battle
came to a close with Satoshi’s victory.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.760
But the path to Monarch Dande
remains a long one.

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:43.180
Who will be his next opponent?

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:09.670
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.670 --> 00:23:10.950
Go!

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:14.290
What a pretty Glacia...

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:17.340
That girl with her...
is she a transfer student?

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:19.380
I wonder what happened.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:21.260
Glacia’s angry.

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:21.960
Huh?

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:26.330
It’s a Blizzard!

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:29.140
Looks like we did it again...

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:31.200
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:33.810
The Ice Queen and Glacia
